# JS bundle ship gate (`app.js` / `app.min.js`)

Owner lesson (**Sep 2026 — production outage**): a greedy regex rewrite **deleted** `renderUnitT`, `renderSuppT`, `renderModT`, and related list renderers. `node --check` still passed (syntax OK); **live site was blank** (`renderUnitT is not defined`, then `TB_TRASH_ICON` TDZ cascade). Users were affected before the owner caught it.

## Hard rule — before saying “done”, “ready”, or “fixed” for any change touching `static/js/app.js`

Run **all** of this in order and fix failures **before** replying:

```text
node --check static/js/app.js
node scripts/minify_app_js.mjs
node scripts/verify_app_js_bundle.mjs
```

If any step fails: **stop**. Do not tell the owner to deploy. Do not say the site will work.

## What `verify_app_js_bundle.mjs` enforces

- `app.js` parses (same as `--check`, but explicit in the gate script)
- Critical **function declarations** still exist (`renderUnitT`, `renderCharT`, `renderSuppT`, `renderModT`, `openDetail`, `applyLang`, `tbApplyLangStatic`, unit grid helpers, etc.)
- `TB_TRASH_ICON` const still declared (late-init cascade symptom when bundle aborts mid-file)
- `app.min.js` exists, is **newer than** `app.js`, and still contains key symbols (production serves min bundle)

Extend `REQUIRED_FUNCTIONS` in the script when adding new top-level browse/boot entrypoints — not ad-hoc one-offs in agent replies.

## Forbidden edit patterns on `app.js`

| Pattern | Why |
|--------|-----|
| `re.sub(..., flags=re.DOTALL)` / greedy regex spanning `function …` | Deleted whole render blocks in Sep 2026 |
| One-off Python “patch” scripts without immediate `verify_app_js_bundle.mjs` | Same failure mode |
| Editing only `app.js` and skipping minify | Live runs `app.min.js` |
| “Syntax check passed” as the only verification | Missing declarations are **not** syntax errors |

**Preferred:** surgical `StrReplace` with unique context, or restore a known-good block from git and re-apply a minimal diff.

## Reply checklist (JS UI changes)

- [ ] `node scripts/verify_app_js_bundle.mjs` — exit 0
- [ ] If owner tests Railway: **fixed locally; not live yet** until they deploy (see `verify-live-before-fixed.mdc`)
- [ ] Mention verify script ran in the reply when JS shipped

